// What the subject's devices recorded in a window around a call: browser
// downloads (with OriginatingDomain and Sha256), files created, copied or
// uploaded, and printing, from the Endpoint workload (Defender for Endpoint /
// Purview endpoint DLP). Set the window from about 30 minutes before the first
// outside contact to two hours after the call ends. An installer, script or
// archive downloaded while the call was live is the finding that decides the
// ticket; a download host on cloudapp.azure.com, blob.core.windows.net or
// s3.amazonaws.com, or with a random-looking file name, is the usual delivery.
// Zero rows: check the tenant has any Workload Endpoint rows at all (Purview
// device onboarding) before reading it as "nothing downloaded".
// Placeholders: {UPN} = the subject's address, lower-cased; {FROM}, {TO} = the
// window as datetime literals.
Office365
| where timestamp between ({FROM} .. {TO})
| where Workload == "Endpoint"
| where tolower(tostring(UserId)) == "{UPN}"
| project timestamp, Operation = tostring(Operation), Device = tolower(tostring(DeviceName)),
    ObjectId = tostring(ObjectId), FileExtension = tostring(FileExtension),
    OriginatingDomain = tostring(OriginatingDomain), Application = tostring(Application),
    Sha256 = tolower(tostring(Sha256))
| summarize dups = count() by timestamp, Operation, Device, ObjectId, FileExtension,
    OriginatingDomain, Application, Sha256
| top 1000 by timestamp desc
